item.text:
**Reused evidence**
None materially beyond the local identity/authority baseline already in the prompt.

**New evidence**
- Party-centered human-development framing from Trọng in January 2022.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Remarks by Party General Secretary Nguyen Phu Trong at National Cultural Conference","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-01-12","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/remarks-by-party-general-secretary-nguyen-phu-trong-at-national-cultural-conference-post220619.vnp","claim":"Trọng said human beings are the subject and centerpiece of development, and that education, training, science and technology are top national policy alongside happy families and gender equality.","locator":"speech text on human development and education","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State news agency reproducing a direct full speech by the party general secretary.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 speech; strongly period-fit for intent and welfare framing.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: this is Trọng speaking as party general secretary; it is attributable to his agenda-setting role, though implementation ran through the CPV-state apparatus.","contrary_evidence":["This is normative rhetoric, not proof of delivery.","It does not by itself show improved outcomes for all groups."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.8","6B.9"]}
- People-centered development in Trọng’s 2022 writings.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"OP-ED: Vietnam working to develop a society truly for people","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-03-14","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/op-ed-vietnam-working-to-develop-a-society-truly-for-people-post223434.vnp","claim":"The op-ed says development for the sake of the people is a core and consistent issue in Trọng's writings, and links that idea to work on the economy, culture, education, health care, and improving material and spiritual life.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State news agency summary of Trọng's own published book and policy framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published in 2022 and directly describes Trọng's welfare-oriented framing in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct but mediated: the claim is about Trọng's writings and ideology; it supports intent more than administrative delivery.","contrary_evidence":["The article is interpretive and still mostly rhetoric.","It does not isolate his personal causal impact on service delivery."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.2","6B.8"]}
- Trọng’s 2022 socio-economic direction-setting.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Party chief gives directions at teleconference between Government, localities","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-01-05","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/party-chief-gives-directions-at-teleconference-between-government-localities-post220249.vnp","claim":"Trọng directed implementation of the Party Central Committee conclusion and the National Assembly's 2022 socio-economic development scheme after reviewing 2021 performance.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a 2022 leadership teleconference, but the claim is broad and not service-specific.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and explicitly about the 2022 policy agenda.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful: this is top-level agenda setting under his party leadership, not proof of direct execution by him.","contrary_evidence":["The source is broad on macro agenda rather than welfare delivery.","It does not show whether implementation later succeeded."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.10"]}
- End-2022 trajectory and shock management.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam gathering momentum for sustainable development: Party leader","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-12-31","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/vietnam-gathering-momentum-for-sustainable-development-party-leader/246404.vnp","claim":"Trọng said Vietnam had to deal with COVID-19, seasonal diseases, and natural disasters in 2022, and that the country achieved and surpassed 14 of 15 targets.","locator":"interview body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct year-end interview with explicit 2022 outcomes and constraints.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published on December 31, 2022 and summarises target-year results.","ruler_attribution":"Direct for year-end evaluation, though the achievements are still system-level rather than personally executed by him alone.","contrary_evidence":["The article is a self-assessment and may overstate government performance.","It does not disaggregate who benefited most."],"lenses":["6B.6","6B.10"]}
- Major health-system investment in the 2022 recovery program.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Resolution on socio-economic recovery and development program passed","publisher":"VGP / baochinhphu.vn","publication_date":"2022-01-11","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/resolution-on-socio-economic-recovery-and-development-program-passed-11122011117055838.htm","claim":"The approved recovery resolution set aside VND 176 trillion for modernizing the grassroots healthcare system, disease-control centers, central hospitals, and related public investment projects.","locator":"resolution funding paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government resolution text with specific budget allocations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly 2022 and squarely within the target-year recovery package.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the resolution was adopted under the CPV-state hierarchy that Trọng chairs politically; implementation was handled by government and ministries.","contrary_evidence":["Budget allocation is not the same as effective disbursement.","The article does not prove equal regional access or quality."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.9"]}
- Broader recovery package for health, security, and institutions.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gov’t proposes US$15 billion economic recovery program","publisher":"VGP / baochinhphu.vn","publication_date":"2022-01-07","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/vgp-news-govt-proposes-us15-billion-economic-recovery-program-111220107094944141.htm","claim":"The recovery program would fund healthcare capacity, social security, business recovery, infrastructure development, and institutional reform.","locator":"program summary paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government program summary with direct policy categories and funding purpose.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly 2022 and tied to the target-year recovery program.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: a government program executed under the CPV-state leadership structure rather than a personal Trọng order.","contrary_evidence":["A funding plan does not guarantee implementation quality.","The package is broad and not all of it is specifically social-welfare targeted."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.6","6B.9"]}
- Health-insurance expansion for vulnerable groups.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Localities urged to raise health insurance coverage to over 95% by 2025","publisher":"VGP / baochinhphu.vn","publication_date":"2022-05-02","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/localities-urged-to-raise-health-insurance-coverage-to-over-95-by-2025-111220502191420801.htm","claim":"The government set 2022 health-insurance coverage at 92.6% and told localities to extend coverage to poor and near-poor households while the education ministry was tasked to get students enrolled by 2023.","locator":"lead and coverage-target bullet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official target-setting document with explicit coverage goals for vulnerable groups.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published in 2022 and directly about 2022 coverage targets.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: national target-setting under the party-state system led by Trọng, though operational responsibility sat with line ministries and provinces.","contrary_evidence":["Targets signal gaps that still needed closing.","The source does not establish actual end-2022 attainment."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.9"]}
- End-2022 health-system results.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Tập trung giải quyết tình trạng thiếu thuốc, vật tư, trang thiết bị y tế","publisher":"Báo Chính phủ / VGP","publication_date":"2023-02-27","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/tap-trung-giai-quyet-tinh-trang-thieu-thuoc-vat-tu-trang-thiet-bi-y-te-102230227141107484.htm","claim":"The health sector said it finished 2022 with 11.1 doctors per 10,000 people, 31 hospital beds per 10,000 people, and 92.03% health-insurance coverage.","locator":"minister's remarks summarizing 2022 sector results","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministerial summary of end-2022 outcomes using concrete sector metrics.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published just after the target year but reporting end-2022 results; acceptable retrospective fit.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: national sector outcomes under the CPV-state led by Trọng, not a uniquely personal causal claim.","contrary_evidence":["Later summary reporting can smooth over regional inequality and service-quality gaps.","It does not attribute outcomes to specific leadership decisions."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.9","6B.10"]}
- UNICEF on education gains and inclusion.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF Viet Nam Key Results 2022","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/unicef-viet-nam-key-results-2022","claim":"UNICEF says 21 million children benefited from improved education policies in 2022, including 700,000 children with disabilities and almost three million children from ethnic communities.","locator":"2022 results - Education section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UNICEF country report with explicit quantitative outcomes and inclusion breakdowns.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The page is explicitly the 2022 results snapshot, even though the publish date is not visible in the snippet.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect country-level outcome evidence under the 2022 party-state system; it does not isolate Trọng personally.","contrary_evidence":["UNICEF also warns that many children remain at risk of being left behind.","The result depends on joint government/partner action, not solely Trọng."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.5","6B.9"]}
- UNICEF on school WASH gaps.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF Viet Nam Key Results 2022","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/unicef-viet-nam-key-results-2022","claim":"UNICEF estimates that 7.7 million children did not have adequate access to clean water and sanitation at school in 2022.","locator":"The Situation of Children in 2022 section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UNICEF country report with a specific country-level estimate and a clear child-welfare nexus.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The page explicitly covers 2022 conditions.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect national-condition evidence; it shows a welfare gap under Trọng's period but not a single-person causal link.","contrary_evidence":["UNICEF also reports some WASH improvements and climate-resilient upgrades.","The estimate is national and does not isolate provincial variance."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.8"]}
- UNICEF on health and nutrition setbacks.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF Viet Nam Key Results 2022","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/unicef-viet-nam-key-results-2022","claim":"UNICEF reports routine immunization fell to 67% in November 2022 and more than 200,000 children experienced severe wasting, with stunting still affecting about one in five under-fives.","locator":"The Situation of Children in 2022 section / Child Survival","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UNICEF country report with specific quantitative child-health indicators and trend comparison.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Explicitly about 2022 child-health conditions.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect period-level outcome; the report reflects national conditions under the 2022 leadership system, not a uniquely personal order.","contrary_evidence":["UNICEF also says Vietnam remained among the five countries with the highest COVID-19 vaccination rates.","The numbers reflect pandemic disruption as well as domestic policy."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.6","6B.10"]}
- UNICEF on child protection and dignity.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF Viet Nam Key Results 2022","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/unicef-viet-nam-key-results-2022","claim":"UNICEF says violence against women and children increased during the pandemic period and that 72.04% of children experienced violent discipline by caregivers.","locator":"The Situation of Children in 2022 / Child Protection section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UNICEF country report with explicit protection and discipline indicators.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The report is explicitly about 2022 and pandemic-era child protection conditions.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect national-system evidence under Trọng's period, not a direct personal incitement or order.","contrary_evidence":["UNICEF also describes child-protection system strengthening efforts.","The page does not attribute every abuse case to central authority."],"lenses":["6B.3","6B.6","6B.8"]}
- World Bank on poverty reduction over the decade.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Vietnam Poverty and Equity Assessment Report","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2023-04-10","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/vietnam/publication/2022-vietnam-poverty-and-equity-assessment-report","claim":"The World Bank says poverty fell from 16.8% to 5% over 2010-2020 and more than 10 million people were lifted out of poverty.","locator":"Main messages","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank assessment with explicit quantitative poverty-reduction findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The report is a 2022 assessment published in 2023, so it is retrospective but still period-relevant.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: this is long-run country performance under the CPV-state system rather than a single-person effect.","contrary_evidence":["The report also says COVID slowed wage growth and job-quality gains.","It covers a decade, not only 2022."],"lenses":["6B.10","6B.2"]}
- World Bank on continuing social-protection and inequality gaps.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Vietnam Poverty and Equity Assessment Report","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2023-04-10","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/vietnam/publication/2022-vietnam-poverty-and-equity-assessment-report","claim":"The report says chronic poverty remains concentrated among ethnic minorities and rural regions, and that COVID exposed weaknesses in social protection for informal workers.","locator":"Policy recommendations / Main messages","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank assessment with explicit distributional and social-protection conclusions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective to 2022 but directly relevant to end-2022 welfare constraints.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect system-level evidence; it shows persistent gaps during Trọng's period but not sole personal responsibility.","contrary_evidence":["The report also notes positive poverty-reduction trends.","The critique is about system coverage and resilience, not universal failure."],"lenses":["6B.3","6B.5","6B.10"]}
- Poverty-line expansion and remaining ethnic-minority gaps.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ten million more people benefit from new poverty reduction policies","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-07-29","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/ten-million-more-people-benefit-from-new-poverty-reduction-policies/234548.vnp","claim":"The new multidimensional poverty line raised the poor-and-near-poor share to 9.35%, meaning an additional 10 million people would benefit from social protection and poverty-reduction policies, while poverty remained high among ethnic minorities.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State news agency report on the official poverty-report launch with direct numerical content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly 2022 and explicitly about policy coverage in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: this is the social-policy environment under Trọng's leadership, not a personal implementation note.","contrary_evidence":["Higher benefit eligibility does not prove actual service delivery.","The article still warns that ethnic-minority poverty remains high."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.10"]}
- Social-policy loans for poor households.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Over 2 million poor households access social policy bank loans","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-01-21","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/over-2-million-poor-households-access-social-policy-bank-loans-post220991.vnp","claim":"More than 2 million poor households accessed loans worth over 80 trillion VND from the Vietnam Bank for Social Policies in 2021.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"State news agency reporting a concrete social-policy finance figure, but the result is one-year-lagged and not independently audited in the snippet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published in 2022, reporting the immediately preceding social-policy reach.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: a system-level social-protection channel under the CPV-state regime led by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["The figure is from 2021 rather than 2022.","Loan access does not guarantee sustained escape from poverty."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.7","6B.10"]}
- Social housing and low-income housing gap.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Construction Minister presents measures to meet housing demand of low income earners","publisher":"VietnamPlus (VNA)","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/construction-minister-presents-measures-to-meet-housing-demand-of-low-income-earners-post243255.vnp","claim":"The minister said social housing had reached 7.79 million square meters versus a 12.5 million square meter target, and the land fund for social housing met just over 36% of demand.","locator":"report on National Assembly Q&A about social housing","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State news agency report on an official parliamentary answer with concrete housing figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly 2022 and about a core welfare domain in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: it reflects national housing delivery under the 2022 leadership system, not a personal Trọng order.","contrary_evidence":["The source highlights a serious delivery gap rather than a completed success.","It is ministerial reporting, not a party-chief speech."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 candidate documents across VietnamPlus/VNA, VGP/Báo Chính phủ, World Bank, UNICEF, and health/social-insurance summaries. I kept 13 distinct URLs and 16 source-claim units.

I rejected or collapsed:
- Duplicate health-insurance and health-sector summaries that repeated the same end-2022 numbers without adding a new claim.
- Duplicate poverty-report mirrors in English and Vietnamese when they repeated the same World Bank conclusions.
- Repeated UNICEF page sections when they did not add a materially distinct claim.
- Out-of-period follow-ups from 2024-2026, unless they explicitly reported end-2022 results and were needed for retrospective context.
- Older non-target material such as 2017 women’s-union coverage and other pre-2022 analogs.
- Foreign-policy, anti-corruption, and general governance pieces that did not materially bear on 6B welfare delivery or human development.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct attribution remains partly indirect: much of the welfare evidence reflects CPV-state policy and sector performance, not Trọng’s personal execution.
- More subnational data would help on regional inequality, ethnic-minority access, WASH, social housing, and child-protection quality.
- Better budget-execution and program-disbursement evidence would help separate announcements from delivery, especially for social housing, health-system modernization, and poverty programs.
